  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>A 4-star campsite of the Homair chain in Saint-Aygulf (Fréjus), set between the Argens river and a long natural beach. The official website puts the beach at about 900 metres, along a pedestrian path that runs beside the Villepey ponds.</p>

      <h2>Conditions for your dog</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>One dog per accommodation; category 1 and 2 dogs are not admitted (official website and Homair).</li>
        <li>Paid supplement: the official website does not publish an amount. Voyages E.Leclerc states €6/day, and the Emmène ton chien directory €7 to €10 per night depending on the range: these figures differ, so ask the campsite for the rate.</li>
        <li>Up-to-date vaccination record and a tag with its name; a lead is compulsory in the campsite (Voyages E.Leclerc, based on the campsite's conditions).</li>
        <li>Homair states that your dog may join you at the campsite's bar and restaurant; Emmène ton chien (Qualidog 2026 label) also mentions a bowl on arrival, poop bags on request and a dog shower.</li>
        <li>The campsite also has a club for renting paddleboards and kayaks on the Argens.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the path to the beach runs along a protected natural area (Villepey ponds): keep your dog on a lead on this stretch.</div>

      <h2>To check before you book</h2>
      <p>The amount of the dog supplement (see above), the current rules on Argens beach (see our beach page) and the dates: the 2026 season is over, the 2027 season is announced from 15/05 to 31/10.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Base Nature François Léotard and its Pacha beach can be reached from the area, for a change of scenery on your walks.</p>
